      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(active-memory): accept max thinking config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users configuring active-memory with `thinking: \"max\"` could have the value rejected by plugin manifest/schema metadata even though the runtime and docs already treat `max` as a valid thinking level.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis updates the active-memory manifest config enum to match the runtime contract and adds a schema regression so the accepted config value stays aligned.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can configure active-memory's maximum thinking level without manifest-driven validation rejecting the documented value.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/active-memory/config.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n- Controlled schema proof: `node --import tsx - <<'EOF' ...` loaded the real active-memory plugin manifest and the SDK JSON-schema validator.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Manifest `thinking` enum includes `max`.\n- Real schema validation accepts `{ enabled: true, agents: [\"main\"], thinking: \"max\" }`.\n- Real schema validation still rejects an invalid value, proving the schema remains restrictive rather than permissive.\n- Controlled proof output: `maxAccepted: true`, `invalidAccepted: false`, `invalidErrorCount: 1`.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/active-memory-thinking-max-20260710",
        "head_sha": "97f831d0cf75ec8e8801c3c6358f97864f0bd55e",
        "author": "llagy007",
